<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Mainpro full yr distribution rises.</title>
<headline>Mainpro full yr distribution rises.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-05-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended March 31 1997</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Distributions		57.20    vs   51.97</p>
<p>    Earnings per unit (cts)  23.32    vs   21.19</p>
<p>Total distributions</p>
<p>per unit</p>
<p>    - interim (cts)	    11.65    vs   10.51</p>
<p>    - final (cts)		11.67    vs   10.68</p>
<p>    - total (cts)		23.32    vs   21.19</p>
<p>Full name: Main Street Property Fund (property)</p>
<p>NOTE - The group said the outlook for 1998 was encouraging. Improved occupancy levels and higher rentals should impact positively on earnings, which are forecast to reflect an improvement over 1997 earnings.</p>
<p>In line with Mainpro's investment strategy, further improvements to the portfolio can be expected in the year ahead. -- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
